// TEST: Mut Arg Partial Application (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4005
// ERROR-CONTAINS: left unsupplied by a partial application
// ============================================================================
// The seam that made the call-site check leak, pinned so it cannot reopen.
//
// A partial application does not stay a partial application: `f(w)` desugars
// to a synthesized lambda whose body calls `f(w, __paN_0)`. The write
// -permission check has to EXEMPT synthesized `__` names -- compiler-generated
// buffers (grad's out-buffer ABI) legitimately pass through `mut` slots -- so
// the caller's real argument arrived at the inner call wearing a `__pa` name
// and the permission was lost exactly at the seam, not enforced.
//
// It was not theoretical: `accum2(w)(g)` mutated a plain `let g` through the
// `mut` slot while the direct `accum2(w, g)` was refused, so the two spellings
// of the same call disagreed. Currying a write-back parameter is refused;
// supplying it directly is the fix, and 088 shows that path working.
// ============================================================================
function accum2(x: Array<Float64 like Idx<3>>, out: mut Array<Float64 like Idx<3>>) -> Float64 = {
    out(0) = x(0)
    out(0)
}
let w = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let mut g = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
let r = accum2(w)(g)
